            "release_date": "2026-11-19T20:32:48",
            "release_notes_markdown": "Local splitscreen for Chivalry 2: 2 to 4 players on one PC. First public release.\n\n**Install:** through the Unchained Launcher, or put `Splitscreen.pak` in the game's `TBL\\Content\\Paks\\` folder. See the [README](https://github.com/rebelancap/Chiv2-Splitscreen#readme) for how to play and the options.\n\n\nFirst public release.\n\n- 2 to 4 local players in offline matches, each with their own view\n- First-person and third-person view per player; bodies, weapons, shields and weapons stuck in shields show correctly in every view\n- Full gamepad combat controls for players 2 to 4, with native gamepad handling (throw chord, aim assist, look sensitivity)\n- L3 tap to throw, and hold L3 to follow the thrown weapon, for every player\n- Loadout menu per player: class, subclass, weapons and team switch; opens on the class you are wearing\n- Per-player HUD: crosshair, enemy name plate, scoreboard, sprint and reload hints, death and spawn messages, damage vignette\n- Rumble on each player's own gamepad\n- Keyboard and mouse mode for player 1 (`sskbm=1`)\n- Player count from the Play Offline Options box (`ssplayers=N`), remembered between sessions\n- One-second warmup instead of the full pre-match wait\n- Fixed: a dead or commending player pulling another player's camera away\n- Fixed: intro music playing once per player\n",
            "tag": "v0.5.0"
        }
